<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">4 events that happened on 13 September, from 1759 to 1996.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/quebec" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quebec.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1759">1759 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">267 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wolfe defeats Montcalm on the Plains of Abraham</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-wolfe">James Wolfe</a> climbed the cliffs above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> and defeated the French in a brief battle. Wolfe was killed and Montcalm mortally wounded; Quebec fell, sealing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The British bombard Fort McHenry in Baltimore</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British warships shelled Fort McHenry for some 25 hours. Seeing the flag still flying at dawn, Francis Scott Key wrote the poem that became 'The Star-Spangled Banner'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1993">1993 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">33 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rabin and Arafat shake hands on the Oslo Accords</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Israel and the PLO signed the Declaration of Principles at the White House, with a historic handshake between Yitzhak Rabin and Yasser Arafat. The deal created Palestinian self-rule, but lasting peace proved elusive.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1996">1996 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tupac Shakur dies after a drive-by shooting</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rapper Tupac Shakur died in Las Vegas aged 25, six days after being shot. One of hip-hop's best-selling and most influential artists, his murder long went unsolved.</p></div></li></ol>
